HST Office: document tab windows on macOS and Windows switch without a window animation, and on
macOS the tabs of a native full screen window stay in its Space.

Switching a document tab shows one top-level window and hides another. On macOS every native full
screen window owns a Space, so the switch played the Space swipe and closing the shown tab left the
full screen Space (the application looked gone). The framework tells vcl which windows are tab group
members (hst_vcl_set_tab_group_member, vcl/source/window/syswin.cxx; no public header changes):

- macOS (vcl/osx/salframe.cxx): members get NSWindowAnimationBehaviorNone; showing a member while
  another member is native full screen adds it to that window's NSWindow tab group (the native tab
  bar is toggled off), so the switch only selects a tab and stays in the Space; hiding a member
  orders it out instead of closing it (a member of a full screen tab group is already hidden by the
  selection; a native full screen window outside a group keeps the close, tdf#161623); after
  hiding, the application stays frontmost and a visible tab becomes key.
- Windows (vcl/win/window/salframe.cxx): DWMWA_TRANSITIONS_FORCEDISABLED for member windows, so the
  DWM fade/zoom of ShowWindow does not play on a switch.
- GTK3: no change (switching measured at 0.1-0.4 s, no gap between hide and show).
- macOS Command-w (vcl/osx/vclnsapp.mm): for a tab it no longer calls performClose: (the title-bar
  close, which closes every tab and ended the application); the .uno:CloseWin accelerator closes
  the shown tab only and the neighbour (or the Start Center) takes over.

Document tab group (all platforms): when a tab is shown and the group has no active tab (the frame
that replaced the Start Center is a member but was never marked active), every other visible task
frame is adopted and the visible previous tab is parked; before, the first document stayed shown
next to the second window.

